(4300952, 617002, 39427, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by grigrigirl:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by AP:</b></div><hr/><i> this is a lovely shot that is rife interpretive potential.  I''d be curious to know whether it is staged? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>It is staged in the sense that I had the couple stand at this spot during their engagement session. Some things cant be staged. I had no idea the older couple was walking hand in hand in the background until I started editing. Are their emotions during this moment staged? I did not instruct them to appreciate each other, to be in love, to close their eyes, to hug or for him to place his head on hers. Life happens and I snap the shutter anyway. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>awesome :)</td>', 'Originally posted by grigrigirl: Originally posted by AP: this is a lovely shot that is rife interpretive potential.  I''d be curious to know whether it is staged?   It is staged in the sense that I had the couple stand at this spot during their engagement session. Some things cant be staged. I had no idea the older couple was walking hand in hand in the background until I started editing. Are their emotions during this moment staged? I did not instruct them to appreciate each other, to be in love, to close their eyes, to hug or for him to place his head on hers. Life happens and I snap the shutter anyway.   awesome :)', '2007-12-08 04:49:17.000000', NULL, 0),
