(4302596, 618004, 50641, '<td valign="top">That thing is so cool.  I''m digging your composition here.  And I like how it''s tethered like a dog without an owner.</td>', 'That thing is so cool.  I''m digging your composition here.  And I like how it''s tethered like a dog without an owner.', '2007-12-09 01:44:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(4302800, 618384, 54033, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by L2:</b></div><hr/><i> Technicals here are well met with regard to exposure, composition, focus, etc.  I don''t mean to hurt your feelings, but this really seems like a standard portrait that you have to know the person to really like the image.  There''s no story - the girl and the cat aren''t interacting -- there''s no true personality captured or anything that makes me wish I was a) at the scene or b) knew the people in it.  Technically though, you got it spot-on.  Artistic merit - although pleasing, it''s rather ordinary. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/><b>Do not listen to what <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/user_id/29009.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/user_id/29009.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/user_id/29009.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=29009" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">L2</a> said above. I loved the cat and the girl because of the photo. I did not have to know them to like them. Great picture. and much under rated.</b><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-12-10 02:08:07.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by L2: Technicals here are well met with regard to exposure, composition, focus, etc.  I don''t mean to hurt your feelings, but this really seems like a standard portrait that you have to know the person to really like the image.  There''s no story - the girl and the cat aren''t interacting -- there''s no true personality captured or anything that makes me wish I was a) at the scene or b) knew the people in it.  Technically though, you got it spot-on.  Artistic merit - although pleasing, it''s rather ordinary.   Do not listen to what  L2 said above. I loved the cat and the girl because of the photo. I did not have to know them to like them. Great picture. and much under rated.', '2007-12-09 05:15:52.000000', '2007-12-10 02:08:07.000000', 0),
(4302834, 617056, 34938, '<td valign="top">Congrats on the D300! Looking forward to getting mine as soon as they are available here in Australia</td>', 'Congrats on the D300! Looking forward to getting mine as soon as they are available here in Australia', '2007-12-09 06:18:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(4302847, 618334, 30982, '<td valign="top">A striking and intricate photograph.  I''m most fond of the blue of the water against the grays of the skies.  Congratulations on a well deserved blue!</td>', 'A striking and intricate photograph.  I''m most fond of the blue of the water against the grays of the skies.  Congratulations on a well deserved blue!', '2007-12-09 06:37:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(4302878, 618562, 30982, '<td valign="top">Nice detail and rich color in the bloom, and a very good diagonal composition.  For a flower shot to do well here, it has to be unique in some way, I think.  This is a good flower shot, but not particularly unique.  There are some artifacts of something in the background that do draw the eye a bit, but I''ll disagree with one commenter about the green in the lower right - I think that provides a nice "support" to the bloom and some good contrasting color.  In the DPC world, there''s a tendency to oversimplify, to have a subject floating somewhat displaced on a pure back blackground that to me artificializes the subject.</td>', 'Nice detail and rich color in the bloom, and a very good diagonal composition.  For a flower shot to do well here, it has to be unique in some way, I think.  This is a good flower shot, but not particularly unique.  There are some artifacts of something in the background that do draw the eye a bit, but I''ll disagree with one commenter about the green in the lower right - I think that provides a nice "support" to the bloom and some good contrasting color.  In the DPC world, there''s a tendency to oversimplify, to have a subject floating somewhat displaced on a pure back blackground that to me artificializes the subject.', '2007-12-09 07:49:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(4302882, 614396, 30982, '<td valign="top">You caught that sliver of light in just the right place - adds the extra something to this to make it that much more than just a good observation shot.  Lovely conversion!</td>', 'You caught that sliver of light in just the right place - adds the extra something to this to make it that much more than just a good observation shot.  Lovely conversion!', '2007-12-09 07:55:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(4302883, 617455, 30982, '<td valign="top">In the "this and $3.50 will get you a Starbucks" category, this was my choice for the red.  Wonderfully seen and I do love the edit.</td>', 'In the "this and $3.50 will get you a Starbucks" category, this was my choice for the red.  Wonderfully seen and I do love the edit.', '2007-12-09 07:56:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(4302907, 618388, 30982, '<td valign="top">Very expansive feeling to this - colors are great.  What probably hurt you in voting is the 640 pixel size limit.  Shots this grand are hard to get across in such a small size.  Doesn''t take away from it''s value as a photograph, just makes it harder to get the score you want.</td>', 'Very expansive feeling to this - colors are great.  What probably hurt you in voting is the 640 pixel size limit.  Shots this grand are hard to get across in such a small size.  Doesn''t take away from it''s value as a photograph, just makes it harder to get the score you want.', '2007-12-09 08:27:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(4302915, 618334, 87551, '<td valign="top">Way cool, i mean COLD  :)</td>', 'Way cool, i mean COLD  :)', '2007-12-09 08:28:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(4302919, 611583, 87551, '<td valign="top">Great shot and very strong colors</td>', 'Great shot and very strong colors', '2007-12-09 08:29:31.000000', NULL, 0),
